          "pause": true,
          "displayType": "poster",
          "buttonOnMobile": false,
          "label": "<p>A 25-year-old man presents with bloody diarrhoea, fever of 39°C, and tenesmus. H</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>A 25-year-old man presents with bloody diarrhoea, fever of 39°C, and tenesmus. His blood pressure is 110/70 mmHg. Which of the following drugs is contraindicated in this patient?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Ciprofloxacin</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Ciprofloxacin is the first-line antibiotic for Shigella dysentery. It targets the invasive organism causing mucosal damage and is indicated, not contraindicated.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Oral rehydration solution</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>ORS is the cornerstone of all diarrhoea management and is always indicated, regardless of the mechanism or severity.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Loperamide</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. Antimotility agents like loperamide are strictly contraindicated in dysentery. Slowing intestinal transit when the mucosa is invaded risks trapping toxins and bacteria, potentially causing toxic megacolon.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Azithromycin</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Azithromycin is an alternative antibiotic for bacterial dysentery and traveller's diarrhoea. It is safe and indicated, not contraindicated.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "The clinical triad of bloody stools, fever, and tenesmus defines dysentery — mucosal invasion. Loperamide slows transit, trapping invasive organisms and their toxins, risking toxic megacolon. It is the one contraindicated drug in this scenario."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Correct — this is a hard safety rule. Never use antimotility agents in dysentery; the risk of toxic megacolon outweighs any symptomatic benefit."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
                "enableRetry": true,
                "enableSolutionsButton": true,
                "enableCheckButton": true,
